Moksha is the constant association of a human's body, senses, mind, and intellect with God. We, free from our daily ego,
free from the impurities of false ego, by dedicating ourselves to the service of God in Krishna consciousness,
can awaken again. When the pure soul accepts false ego, then it has to
endure physical suffering. In pure Krishna consciousness, by accepting oneself as an eternal servant of Lord Krishna, false ego can be automatically conquered. Immeasurable, yet manifested in many forms,
In the mind, speech, life force, and body actions.
