Although false ego has no real basis, it is seen in many forms—as in mind, speech, life force, and the functions of the body. But through the worship of an authentic guru,
with the divine sword of knowledge, the serious saint cuts off this false identity
and resides in this world, freed from all material attachments.
Meaning: Multiform-multiformed, "targeted in many forms," also indicates that false ego also manifests in the belief that a person is a deity, a great man, a beautiful woman, a sorrowful one,
a worker, a tiger, a bird, an insect, etc. Due to false ego, the pure soul considers any physical covering
as its ultimate soul, but such ignorance can be removed by the method described in this verse. Knowledge, discrimination, and the Nigama-astuta-papa-cha.
